# Note: ~/.gnupg/gpg-load-passphrase.sh used to be invoked here to preload
# passphrases from the macOS Keychain into gpg-agent at shell startup. Dropped
# because gpg-agent's own caching (default-cache-ttl 86400, max-cache-ttl
# 2592000 in ~/.gnupg/gpg-agent.conf) already covers this — first sign/decrypt
# after a reboot prompts via pinentry once, then silent for up to 30 days.
# The preload script also depended on per-keychain-item ACLs that drifted under
# macOS Sequoia, causing a `security find-generic-password` permission prompt
# per shell (per tmux pane!) instead of the intended silent read. The script
# itself is still on disk for manual runs after a reboot if desired.

